---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="How this site handles your data." heroAnimation="cipher">
  <section class="relative flex min-h-[50dvh] items-center px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="relative z-10 mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <h1 class="text-text">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="text-text-muted mt-2">How this site handles your data.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8" data-pagefind-body>
    <div class="text-text space-y-6 leading-relaxed">
      <h2>Data Collection</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted">
        This site uses <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong>, gated behind a consent banner. No tracking occurs before you
        grant consent. When analytics is enabled, aggregate traffic data (page views, scroll depth, reading time) and
        basic device context (language, timezone, screen size) are collected. No data is sold.
      </p>
      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted">
        If you grant <strong>advertising</strong> consent (a separate toggle in the banner), two ad scripts load:
        <strong>Google AdSense</strong> (publisher ID <code>ca-pub-6275306310835906</code>) and the
        <strong>LinkedIn Insight Tag</strong>. Both set third-party cookies managed by Google and LinkedIn respectively
        and are used for ads and ad measurement. Declining advertising keeps both scripts off entirely.
      </p>
      <h2>Local Storage &amp; Cookies</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted">
        Three items are stored in your browser's <strong>localStorage</strong>: a theme preference (<code>theme</code>),
        your consent choices (<code>adrianwedd_consent</code>), and — only if you enable personalisation — a visitor
        memory (<code>adrianwedd_visitor</code>) holding a visit count, a last-visit timestamp, up to 50 recently viewed
        page paths, and the hostname of the site that referred you. It never leaves your device. All of these persist
        until you clear your browser data.
      </p>
      <p class="text-text-muted">
        The consent banner also sets one first-party cookie (<code>consent</code>, 1-year expiry) recording which
        categories you enabled. If you grant consent, GA4 (analytics) and AdSense/LinkedIn (advertising) set their own
        third-party cookies.
      </p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted">
        Questions about privacy? <a href="/contact/" class="text-accent hover:underline">Get in touch</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
